    {
      "id": "P01",
      "name": "Local Development Platform",
      "status": "completed",
      "stages": [
        {
          "id": "FPA-P01-S01",
          "title": "Accept local development platform ADR",
          "status": "completed",
          "dependencies": [
            "FPA-P00-S03"
          ],
          "notes": [
            "ADR-0003 accepted 2026-08-01 (git tag phase-1-s01). Stage scope was solely ADR acceptance, so the ADR commit is the stage-completion commit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "FPA-P01-S02",
          "title": "Scaffold web, API and image-analysis applications",
          "status": "completed",
          "dependencies": [
            "FPA-P01-S01"
          ],
          "notes": [
            "React/Vite, Laravel and FastAPI application skeletons implemented with health endpoints, service tests and accepted quality tooling on 2026-08-01.",
            "Formatting, linting, type checks, tests, production web build, manifest/lock validation, dependency audits and independent runtime health checks passed. Stage completed on the approved application-scaffold commit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "FPA-P01-S03",
          "title": "Add local infrastructure services",
          "status": "completed",
          "dependencies": [
            "FPA-P01-S02"
          ],
          "notes": [
            "Docker Compose now runs the web, API and image-analysis applications with PostgreSQL, Redis, LocalStack S3/SQS and Mailpit using health-gated startup, named volumes and safe local defaults.",
            "Configuration validation, application quality gates, restart verification, service health checks and direct plus Laravel-level PostgreSQL, Redis, S3 and SQS smoke checks passed. Stage completed on the approved reproducible-infrastructure commit on 2026-08-01."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "FPA-P01-S04",
          "title": "Add baseline observability",
          "status": "completed",
          "dependencies": [
            "FPA-P01-S03"
          ],
          "notes": [
            "OpenTelemetry traces and metrics now flow from Laravel and FastAPI through a dedicated Collector to Grafana LGTM; structured logs and HTTP responses carry operational identifiers.",
            "A correlated synthetic SQS path verifies W3C trace-context propagation by comparing producer and consumer trace IDs.",
            "Phase-end review (full stack booted and every verification command re-run live, not just re-read) found and Codex fixed two issues: scripts/smoke-infrastructure.sh was not idempotent (stale undeleted SQS messages could fail a later run -- fixed and confirmed idempotent across three consecutive runs), and POST /api/observability/synthetic-upload was reachable unauthenticated in any environment -- now gated to local/testing at both route registration and inside the handler. The synthetic consumer's message-receive logic was also extracted into a tested function, removing an unhandled-IndexError risk on an empty poll.",
            "Repository scaffold, local infrastructure and observability baseline verified and Phase 1 acceptance gate passed on 2026-08-01. FPA-P01-S04 and Phase 1 completed on the same completion commit."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
